@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix ies:  <http://ies.data.gov.uk/ontology/ies4#> .
@prefix obo:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/> .

# Manual semantic curation, BFO <-> IES
#
# These two mappings were found by reading definitions directly rather than
# through compare_structures.py's structural matching (which, even after
# formalizing IES's definitions into restriction axioms, only ever turned up
# coincidental structural matches against BFO's top-level categories; see
# FINDINGS.md). Both assertions use rdfs:subClassOf rather than
# owl:equivalentClass, since in both cases the BFO class is strictly broader
# than the IES class, not identical to it.

ies:Event rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000015 .
# ies:Event ("an activity or incident... that occurred/started at a specific
# point in time") matches BFO's process (an occurrent with participants).
# Not every BFO process is an IES Event (process is far broader), so this is
# subsumption, not equivalence.

ies:Entity rdfs:subClassOf obo:BFO_0000004 .
# ies:Entity ("a tangible thing like a Person, a Communications Device, or a
# Location") is mapped to BFO's independent continuant rather than material
# entity specifically, since IES's own example "Location" is not made of
# matter and so would not qualify as a material entity in BFO's sense.
